text Paying attention to whether there is anyone around us, I kiss her when we part ways.
text Fujibayashi kisses me back as well.
text Her face flushes so red that I could tell even under the setting sun. She then bows and walks away.
text For a moment, I stand there watching her back growing farther and farther away.
text The breeze lightly touches my lips, where a warm sensation lingers.
text Even though it is already spring, the breeze feels cold... and causes me to feel awfully lonely.
